1
00:00:03,718 --> 00:00:04,844
KATARA: Water...

2
00:00:04,928 --> 00:00:06,262
Earth...

3
00:00:06,346 --> 00:00:08,223
Fire...

4
00:00:08,306 --> 00:00:10,642
Air.

5
00:00:10,725 --> 00:00:12,018
Long ago...

6
00:00:12,101 --> 00:00:14,729
The four nations lived
together in harmony.

7
00:00:14,812 --> 00:00:19,067
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

8
00:00:19,150 --> 00:00:23,154
Only the Avatar, master of
all four elements, could stop them.

9
00:00:23,613 --> 00:00:25,198
But when the world
needed him most

10
00:00:25,281 --> 00:00:27,408
he vanished.

11
00:00:27,492 --> 00:00:30,828
A hundred years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar...

12
00:00:30,912 --> 00:00:32,664
An airbender named Aang.

13
00:00:32,872 --> 00:00:35,208
And although his airbending
skills are great

14
00:00:35,291 --> 00:00:37,794
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

15
00:00:37,877 --> 00:00:39,045
AANG: Oof.

16
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:42,632
But I believe
Aang can save the world.

17
00:00:42,757 --> 00:00:44,175
( ♪... )

18
00:00:48,054 --> 00:00:50,306
( MAN READING )

19
00:00:50,473 --> 00:00:51,849
What about the invasion?

20
00:00:51,975 --> 00:00:54,394
We'll join up with my dad
and the invasion force

21
00:00:54,477 --> 00:00:56,145
on the day of the eclipse.

22
00:00:56,271 --> 00:00:58,189
SOKKA: Keep quiet.

23
00:00:58,314 --> 00:01:01,109
We're in enemy territory.

24
00:01:01,234 --> 00:01:04,279
KATARA: What we need is some
new clothes.

25
00:01:04,404 --> 00:01:06,322
AANG: Yeah, blending in
is better than hiding out.

26
00:01:06,447 --> 00:01:08,324
If we get Fire Nation disguises

27
00:01:08,449 --> 00:01:11,160
we'll be just as safe
as we would be hiding in a cave.

28
00:01:11,286 --> 00:01:13,371
Ta-da,
normal kid.

29
00:01:14,455 --> 00:01:15,456
KATARA: How do I look?

30
00:01:21,045 --> 00:01:25,133
( ♪... )

31
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:30,722
( APPA GRUNTING )

32
00:01:30,847 --> 00:01:32,223
Momo?

33
00:01:32,348 --> 00:01:33,891
( MOMO CHATTERING )

34
00:01:34,017 --> 00:01:37,145
Oh, Momo?

35
00:01:37,270 --> 00:01:39,314
Ah. ( LAUGHS )

36
00:01:39,439 --> 00:01:43,151
You found me, buddy.

37
00:01:43,276 --> 00:01:45,403
Hey, guys, I think
this river's polluted.

38
00:01:45,528 --> 00:01:47,155
( INHALES, GRUNTS )

39
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:50,867
( ALL GROANING )

40
00:01:50,992 --> 00:01:54,704
( SPITS )

41
00:01:54,829 --> 00:01:58,082
Well, that explains why I can't
catch a fish around here.

42
00:01:58,166 --> 00:02:02,211
Because normally my fishing
skills are... Off the hook.

43
00:02:02,295 --> 00:02:04,464
Get it,
like a fishing hook?

44
00:02:04,672 --> 00:02:07,050
Too bad your skills aren't
on the hook.

45
00:02:07,175 --> 00:02:11,346
( ALL LAUGHING )

46
00:02:11,471 --> 00:02:15,058
It looks like we'll need to go
somewhere else to get food.

47
00:02:15,141 --> 00:02:17,977
Assuming that'll fit into
Sokka's master schedule.

48
00:02:18,144 --> 00:02:20,313
Hm... It's doable.

49
00:02:20,438 --> 00:02:22,690
But that means only two
potty breaks today.

50
00:02:22,815 --> 00:02:25,234
Hey, maybe we can
get food there.

51
00:02:30,198 --> 00:02:32,700
Now you look just like
a little hill with horns.

52
00:02:32,825 --> 00:02:34,285
Bye, buddy.

53
00:02:34,410 --> 00:02:37,705
( APPA SNORTS, MOMO CHATTERS )

54
00:02:37,830 --> 00:02:40,083
TOPH: I don't feel anything.

55
00:02:40,208 --> 00:02:41,626
Where's this village?

56
00:02:41,751 --> 00:02:43,336
It's in the middle
of the river.

57
00:02:43,461 --> 00:02:44,796
MAN: Sure is.

58
00:02:44,921 --> 00:02:46,297
My name's Dock.

59
00:02:46,422 --> 00:02:47,882
Mind if I ask who you are?

60
00:02:48,007 --> 00:02:52,053
We're, um, from the Earth
Kingdom colonies.

61
00:02:52,178 --> 00:02:54,013
DOCK: Wow, colonials.

62
00:02:54,347 --> 00:02:56,724
Hop on, I'll give you a ride
into town.

63
00:02:59,435 --> 00:03:01,479
KATARA: Why do you guys
live on the river?

64
00:03:01,604 --> 00:03:03,481
Because we're a fishing town.

65
00:03:03,606 --> 00:03:06,317
At least that's how it was
before the factory moved in.

66
00:03:06,442 --> 00:03:09,070
Army makes their metal there.

67
00:03:09,195 --> 00:03:12,365
Moved in a few years ago and
started gunking up our river.

68
00:03:12,490 --> 00:03:15,284
Now our little village is
struggling to survive.

69
00:03:21,290 --> 00:03:24,919
AANG: Thanks for the ride.

70
00:03:25,044 --> 00:03:27,255
KATARA: Look at this place.

71
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:29,006
It's so sad.

72
00:03:29,132 --> 00:03:32,009
We have to do something to help.

73
00:03:32,135 --> 00:03:34,595
No, we can't waste
our time here.

74
00:03:34,721 --> 00:03:37,306
We have a bigger mission
that we need to stay focused on.

75
00:03:37,432 --> 00:03:39,726
These people are on their own.

76
00:03:39,851 --> 00:03:43,479
These people are starving,
but you turn your back on them?

77
00:03:43,604 --> 00:03:46,149
How can you be so cold
and heartless?

78
00:03:46,274 --> 00:03:49,318
I'm not turning my back,
I'm just being realistic.

79
00:03:49,444 --> 00:03:52,488
We can't go around helping every
rinky-dink town we wander into.

80
00:03:52,613 --> 00:03:55,283
We'll be helping them all
by taking out the Fire Lord.

81
00:03:55,408 --> 00:03:56,909
TOPH: Hey, loudmouth...

82
00:03:57,034 --> 00:03:59,120
Maybe we should be
a little quieter

83
00:03:59,245 --> 00:04:02,081
When we talk about taking out
the Fire Lord.

84
00:04:02,206 --> 00:04:04,375
Come on, Katara,
be reasonable about this.

85
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:06,252
You know our mission
has to come first.

86
00:04:06,377 --> 00:04:08,796
I guess so.

87
00:04:08,921 --> 00:04:10,423
Let's just get
what we need and go.

88
00:04:17,221 --> 00:04:19,390
( BELL RINGS )
Hey, Dock, you work here too?

89
00:04:19,515 --> 00:04:21,934
I'm not Dock, I'm Shoe.

90
00:04:22,059 --> 00:04:24,020
Dock's my brother.

91
00:04:24,145 --> 00:04:25,646
But we just saw you.

92
00:04:25,772 --> 00:04:27,774
You're even wearing
the same clothes.

93
00:04:27,899 --> 00:04:29,859
The only difference is your hat.

94
00:04:29,984 --> 00:04:33,154
Dock works on the Docks,
that's why they call him "Dock."

95
00:04:33,279 --> 00:04:36,199
And I work in the shop,
that's why they call me "Shoe."

96
00:04:36,324 --> 00:04:37,492
I don't get it.

97
00:04:37,617 --> 00:04:40,203
Me neither.

98
00:04:40,328 --> 00:04:42,246
What can I get you?

99
00:04:42,371 --> 00:04:43,498
( FLIES BUZZING )

100
00:04:43,623 --> 00:04:45,625
Hey, I'll give you
a special deal.

101
00:04:45,750 --> 00:04:50,505
If you buy three fish,
I'll throw in a clam for free.

102
00:04:50,630 --> 00:04:52,423
( SQUISH )

103
00:04:52,548 --> 00:04:55,843
-( BOTH GROAN )
- We'll just take the fish.

104
00:04:55,968 --> 00:04:59,722
Mind telling your brother
we need a ride back to shore?

105
00:04:59,847 --> 00:05:01,432
Hey, colonials.

106
00:05:01,557 --> 00:05:03,559
My brother says you need a lift.

107
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:10,107
Can you spare some food?

108
00:05:10,233 --> 00:05:13,152
I wish I could help more.

109
00:05:25,206 --> 00:05:29,669
( WATER SPLASHING )

110
00:05:29,794 --> 00:05:32,964
Our detour into town today
has completely thrown off our schedule.

111
00:05:33,089 --> 00:05:37,093
It's gonna take some serious
finagling to get us back on track.

112
00:05:37,218 --> 00:05:40,513
Finagle away,
o schedule master.

113
00:05:40,638 --> 00:05:41,681
Well, for starters, it looks like we'll

114
00:05:41,764 --> 00:05:43,724
need to wake up 43 minutes earlier
every day.

115
00:05:43,850 --> 00:05:45,935
KATARA: 43 minutes?

116
00:05:46,060 --> 00:05:48,062
Look, we only have a few weeks to get to

117
00:05:48,145 --> 00:05:50,565
the Fire Lord in time for the invasion
and the eclipse

118
00:05:50,690 --> 00:05:52,692
which, by the way,
only lasts for eight minutes.

119
00:05:52,817 --> 00:05:54,610
And we just lost a whole day.

120
00:05:54,735 --> 00:05:57,405
So if we want to make up
the time and stay on schedule

121
00:05:57,530 --> 00:05:58,823
we have to wake up early.

122
00:05:58,948 --> 00:06:01,284
Well, I'm not
waking up early.

123
00:06:01,409 --> 00:06:04,453
Or we could just cut out
all of our eating breaks.

124
00:06:04,579 --> 00:06:06,414
- What?
- No way. Forget it.

125
00:06:06,539 --> 00:06:08,708
I got it, how's this?

126
00:06:08,833 --> 00:06:11,502
From now on, we'll take
food breaks and potty breaks

127
00:06:11,627 --> 00:06:13,045
at the same time.

128
00:06:13,170 --> 00:06:14,380
Ew.

129
00:06:14,505 --> 00:06:16,757
Hey, it might be gross,
but it's efficient.

130
00:06:16,883 --> 00:06:19,552
Either way, we have to
leave here first thing tomorrow morning.

131
00:06:25,683 --> 00:06:28,144
( APPA GROANING )

132
00:06:28,269 --> 00:06:29,353
What's the matter, Katara?

133
00:06:29,478 --> 00:06:31,397
I think Appa's sick.

134
00:06:31,522 --> 00:06:34,066
What, Appa's sick?
That's awful.

135
00:06:34,191 --> 00:06:37,528
TOPH: Wow, Sokka, I didn't
realize you cared so much.

136
00:06:37,653 --> 00:06:39,322
Of course I care.

137
00:06:39,447 --> 00:06:44,493
I might as well just
throw our schedule away now.

138
00:06:44,619 --> 00:06:49,040
And I'm concerned because my
big, furry friend doesn't feel well.

139
00:06:49,165 --> 00:06:50,499
TOPH: He must've gotten sick

140
00:06:50,625 --> 00:06:52,251
from being in the
polluted water.

141
00:06:52,376 --> 00:06:53,586
AANG: He doesn't look sick.

142
00:06:53,711 --> 00:06:55,379
Are you OK, buddy?

143
00:06:55,504 --> 00:06:57,506
( GROANS )

144
00:06:57,632 --> 00:06:59,175
His tongue is purple.

145
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:00,676
That can't be good.

146
00:07:00,801 --> 00:07:02,386
Katara, can you heal him?

147
00:07:02,511 --> 00:07:04,430
It looks like he needs
some medicine.

148
00:07:04,555 --> 00:07:07,850
Maybe we can find
the right herbs in town.

149
00:07:11,479 --> 00:07:15,232
TOPH: Is it just me, or
does this place seem different?

150
00:07:15,358 --> 00:07:18,027
AANG: Yeah,
are the people happier?

151
00:07:18,152 --> 00:07:23,532
( CHILD LAUGHING )

152
00:07:23,658 --> 00:07:26,035
SOKKA: Hey, Shoe, what's
going on with everyone today?

153
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:29,997
Ah, something amazing happened
last night.

154
00:07:30,122 --> 00:07:34,210
Food was delivered to our village by
a mysterious and wonderful person.

155
00:07:34,335 --> 00:07:36,504
The Painted Lady.

156
00:07:36,629 --> 00:07:37,630
The painted who now?

157
00:07:37,713 --> 00:07:39,590
The Painted Lady.

158
00:07:39,715 --> 00:07:41,884
She's part of our town's lore.

159
00:07:42,009 --> 00:07:43,678
They say she's a river spirit

160
00:07:43,803 --> 00:07:46,597
who watches over our town
in times of need.

161
00:07:46,722 --> 00:07:48,474
I always thought she was
just a legend.

162
00:07:48,599 --> 00:07:51,060
Until now.

163
00:07:51,185 --> 00:07:52,728
SOKKA: See, we don't need to help
these people,

164
00:07:52,812 --> 00:07:54,730
they already have someone to help them.

165
00:07:54,855 --> 00:07:57,274
All we need is medicine
for our sick friend.

166
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:58,651
SHOE: Medicine?

167
00:07:58,776 --> 00:08:02,113
Sorry, all the medicine we have
goes to the factory.

168
00:08:02,238 --> 00:08:05,241
That's why there's so many
sick people in our village.

169
00:08:05,366 --> 00:08:08,119
Looks like we need to stay
another night so Appa can rest.

170
00:08:08,244 --> 00:08:10,329
( SIGHS ) I guess you're right.

171
00:08:10,454 --> 00:08:12,915
You got any more food to sell?

172
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:16,544
Would you like the one-headed
fish or the two-headed fish?

173
00:08:16,669 --> 00:08:19,630
Two-headed.

174
00:08:19,755 --> 00:08:22,174
What, you get more
for your money that way.

175
00:08:22,299 --> 00:08:23,551
( ALL GROAN )

176
00:08:23,676 --> 00:08:25,678
( FLIES BUZZING )

177
00:08:32,643 --> 00:08:34,645
( ♪... )

178
00:09:03,090 --> 00:09:06,594
Thank you, Painted Lady.

179
00:09:06,719 --> 00:09:09,513
( WATER SPLASHES )

180
00:09:18,272 --> 00:09:20,316
Hi, Dock, is Shoe around?

181
00:09:20,441 --> 00:09:24,945
Let me check... ( WHISTLING )

182
00:09:25,071 --> 00:09:27,656
( WHISTLING ) Hey there,
back again, are you?

183
00:09:27,782 --> 00:09:29,408
We need more food.

184
00:09:29,533 --> 00:09:33,412
Our friend is still sick and we
can't leave until he's better.

185
00:09:33,537 --> 00:09:35,456
Oh, well,
that's too bad.

186
00:09:35,581 --> 00:09:37,166
Maybe if you guys are lucky

187
00:09:37,291 --> 00:09:39,210
the Painted Lady will
visit you in the night

188
00:09:39,335 --> 00:09:40,419
and heal your friend.

189
00:09:40,544 --> 00:09:42,880
And maybe she'll cook us
a midnight snack

190
00:09:43,005 --> 00:09:44,465
and we'll all have a sing-along.

191
00:09:44,590 --> 00:09:46,926
Yeah, maybe.

192
00:09:47,051 --> 00:09:49,261
You know, last night
she visited us again.

193
00:09:49,386 --> 00:09:51,472
Healed most of our sick folks.

194
00:09:51,597 --> 00:09:53,557
AANG: Is that why this place
seems so festive?

195
00:09:53,682 --> 00:09:57,144
SHOE: Yep, it's all because of
the Painted Lady.

196
00:09:57,269 --> 00:10:01,315
KATARA: Can you believe how much an entire
village can be affected by one lady?

197
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:02,983
I mean, spirit?

198
00:10:03,109 --> 00:10:04,735
Well, I hope she returns
every night.

199
00:10:04,860 --> 00:10:07,446
Otherwise this place would go
right back to the way it was.

200
00:10:07,530 --> 00:10:09,240
Why would you say that?

201
00:10:09,323 --> 00:10:11,158
Look how much better off
these people are.

202
00:10:11,242 --> 00:10:14,245
Yeah, now, but without her, they wouldn't
be able to fend for themselves.

203
00:10:14,495 --> 00:10:16,580
If she really wanted to help

204
00:10:16,705 --> 00:10:19,500
she would use her spirit magic
to blow up that factory.

205
00:10:19,625 --> 00:10:23,546
Ooh... ( IMITATES EXPLOSION )

206
00:10:23,671 --> 00:10:26,006
Spirit magic doesn't work
that way, Sokka.

207
00:10:26,132 --> 00:10:31,595
It's more like...
Whoo... ( IMITATES EXPLOSION )

208
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:34,473
-( LAUGHING )
- Whoo...

209
00:11:00,291 --> 00:11:04,628
( MOMO CHATTERING )

210
00:11:04,753 --> 00:11:07,298
What's the matter, buddy?

211
00:11:07,423 --> 00:11:10,509
It's her.

212
00:11:10,634 --> 00:11:12,178
Hello, Painted Lady spirit.

213
00:11:21,645 --> 00:11:24,607
Excuse me,
I don't mean to bother you

214
00:11:24,732 --> 00:11:28,402
but my friend's sick and we're
on kind of a tight schedule.

215
00:11:28,485 --> 00:11:32,615
Wait, but I'm the great bridge
between your world and mine.

216
00:11:32,865 --> 00:11:38,037
( ICE CRACKLING )

217
00:11:39,038 --> 00:11:41,916
AANG: I know Hei Bai,
we're close personal friends.

218
00:11:54,053 --> 00:11:55,512
Hey.

219
00:11:55,638 --> 00:11:57,640
( GRUNTS )

220
00:12:01,393 --> 00:12:06,690
( PANTING )

221
00:12:06,774 --> 00:12:08,859
( GASPS )

222
00:12:08,943 --> 00:12:09,944
My name's Aang.

223
00:12:10,027 --> 00:12:13,113
I'm the Avatar.

224
00:12:13,197 --> 00:12:15,491
Well, hello, Avatar.

225
00:12:15,574 --> 00:12:18,869
I wish I could talk,
but I am very busy.

226
00:12:19,161 --> 00:12:20,496
Yeah, me too.

227
00:12:20,579 --> 00:12:23,332
I hate that.

228
00:12:23,415 --> 00:12:25,751
You know, you're really pretty
for a spirit.

229
00:12:25,834 --> 00:12:27,419
I don't get to meet too many spirits,

230
00:12:27,503 --> 00:12:30,297
but the ones I do meet...
Not very attractive.

231
00:12:30,839 --> 00:12:33,259
( CHUCKLES ) Thank you, but...

232
00:12:33,384 --> 00:12:36,262
You seem familiar, too.

233
00:12:36,387 --> 00:12:38,055
A lot of people say that.

234
00:12:38,180 --> 00:12:41,016
No, you really seem familiar.

235
00:12:41,141 --> 00:12:45,104
Look, I really should
get going.

236
00:12:48,774 --> 00:12:51,026
Katara?

237
00:12:51,151 --> 00:12:52,403
Hi, Aang.

238
00:12:52,528 --> 00:12:55,239
You're the Painted Lady?
But how?

239
00:12:55,364 --> 00:12:58,659
I wasn't at first, I was just
trying to help the village.

240
00:12:58,784 --> 00:13:00,995
But since everyone thought
that's who I was anyway...

241
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:05,916
I guess I just kind of
became her.

242
00:13:06,041 --> 00:13:08,252
So you've been sneaking out
at night?

243
00:13:08,377 --> 00:13:10,713
Wait, is Appa even sick?

244
00:13:10,838 --> 00:13:14,425
He might be sick of the purple
berries I've been feeding him

245
00:13:14,550 --> 00:13:16,677
but other than that, he's fine.

246
00:13:16,802 --> 00:13:19,722
I can't believe you lied to
everyone so you could help these people.

247
00:13:19,847 --> 00:13:22,141
I'm sorry,
I know I shouldn't have.

248
00:13:22,266 --> 00:13:23,684
No, I think it's great.

249
00:13:23,809 --> 00:13:26,562
You're like a secret hero.

250
00:13:26,687 --> 00:13:28,647
Well, if you want to help...

251
00:13:28,772 --> 00:13:32,109
There's one more thing
I have to do.

252
00:13:41,035 --> 00:13:43,370
You want to destroy
this factory?

253
00:13:43,454 --> 00:13:46,540
Yes, Sokka was just kidding,
but he was right.

254
00:13:46,623 --> 00:13:50,127
Getting rid of this factory is the only
way to help these people permanently.

255
00:14:14,735 --> 00:14:16,695
( ♪... )

256
00:14:43,514 --> 00:14:44,973
Ha-ha...
( IMITATES EXPLOSION )

257
00:14:45,057 --> 00:14:48,477
Shh, we don't want to
wake Sokka.

258
00:14:48,811 --> 00:14:50,646
Hi... Sokka.

259
00:14:50,896 --> 00:14:53,649
We were just out
on a morning walk.

260
00:14:53,941 --> 00:14:55,067
Oh, really?

261
00:14:55,275 --> 00:14:58,487
A morning walk?

262
00:15:01,782 --> 00:15:03,367
I know you're the Painted Lady.

263
00:15:03,492 --> 00:15:05,369
I know you've been sneaking out
at night.

264
00:15:05,494 --> 00:15:07,287
And I know you've been lying about Appa

265
00:15:07,371 --> 00:15:09,873
and feeding him
purple-izing-tongue berries.

266
00:15:09,998 --> 00:15:12,751
- Ah.
-( MOMO CHATTERS )

267
00:15:12,876 --> 00:15:15,212
Katara, what you did put our
whole mission in jeopardy.

268
00:15:15,337 --> 00:15:19,842
We're leaving right now.

269
00:15:19,967 --> 00:15:22,052
And how long did you
know about this?

270
00:15:22,177 --> 00:15:24,972
Hey, I just found out
this morning.

271
00:15:46,243 --> 00:15:47,870
What's going on?

272
00:15:47,995 --> 00:15:50,080
Fire Nation soldiers are
heading to the village.

273
00:15:50,205 --> 00:15:51,790
What did you do?

274
00:15:51,915 --> 00:15:53,792
I kind of destroyed
their factory.

275
00:15:53,917 --> 00:15:55,043
You what?

276
00:15:55,169 --> 00:15:58,005
- It was your idea.
- I was joking.

277
00:15:58,130 --> 00:16:01,341
I also said to use spirit magic
and made funny noises.

278
00:16:01,467 --> 00:16:03,886
( GROANS ) Did you even
think this through?

279
00:16:04,011 --> 00:16:05,804
The army's gonna blame
the villagers.

280
00:16:05,929 --> 00:16:07,806
They're headed there right now
to get revenge.

281
00:16:07,931 --> 00:16:09,558
Well, what was I supposed to do?

282
00:16:09,683 --> 00:16:11,351
Leave, do nothing.

283
00:16:12,686 --> 00:16:13,687
No.

284
00:16:13,770 --> 00:16:16,982
I will never, ever turn my back
on people who need me.

285
00:16:17,483 --> 00:16:20,027
I'm going down to the village

286
00:16:20,110 --> 00:16:23,030
And I am gonna do
whatever I can.

287
00:16:27,034 --> 00:16:28,076
Wait.

288
00:16:28,202 --> 00:16:30,329
I'm coming too.

289
00:16:30,454 --> 00:16:32,581
I thought you didn't
want to help.

290
00:16:32,706 --> 00:16:36,210
You need me, and I will never
turn my back on you.

291
00:16:36,335 --> 00:16:40,756
Sokka, you really do have
a heart.

292
00:16:40,881 --> 00:16:44,468
He really does have a heart,
doesn't he?

293
00:16:44,593 --> 00:16:45,886
( GRUNTS )

294
00:16:46,011 --> 00:16:48,263
( ♪... )

295
00:16:54,561 --> 00:16:57,022
( ♪... )

296
00:16:57,147 --> 00:16:59,566
I thought we could live
as neighbors in peace

297
00:16:59,691 --> 00:17:01,235
but I guess I was wrong.

298
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:03,987
You steal our food,
our medicine...

299
00:17:04,112 --> 00:17:06,198
And then you destroy
our factory.

300
00:17:06,323 --> 00:17:08,742
We didn't do any of that.

301
00:17:08,867 --> 00:17:11,745
Yeah, the Painted Lady
brought us food.

302
00:17:11,870 --> 00:17:14,623
She's the one that healed
our sick, not your medicine.

303
00:17:14,748 --> 00:17:19,586
Oh, right, the mysterious
Painted Lady did it.

304
00:17:19,711 --> 00:17:24,716
And I suppose she drew the army
emblem on your containers, too.

305
00:17:24,841 --> 00:17:26,260
( CROWD GASPS )

306
00:17:26,385 --> 00:17:29,805
This is a town of thieves
and liars.

307
00:17:29,930 --> 00:17:32,891
( GRUNTS )

308
00:17:33,016 --> 00:17:37,646
Where's your Painted Lady now?

309
00:17:37,771 --> 00:17:40,524
We're going to cure the world
of this wretched village.

310
00:18:00,836 --> 00:18:04,673
Light it again.

311
00:18:04,798 --> 00:18:07,593
Look at that,
where's it coming from?

312
00:18:07,718 --> 00:18:09,261
I don't know.

313
00:18:09,386 --> 00:18:11,638
Something strange is going on.

314
00:18:11,763 --> 00:18:13,890
( DISTANT ROARING )

315
00:18:14,016 --> 00:18:15,684
( WHISPERS )
It's the Painted Lady.

316
00:18:15,809 --> 00:18:17,644
( SINGSONG ) She's coming.

317
00:18:17,769 --> 00:18:19,605
There is no Painted Lady.

318
00:18:19,730 --> 00:18:23,358
( ROARING AND LOUD THUDS )

319
00:18:33,327 --> 00:18:35,579
( PLAYING EERIE TUNE )

320
00:18:39,833 --> 00:18:42,753
- What is that sound?
- Maybe it is her.

321
00:19:00,103 --> 00:19:01,938
Do something.

322
00:19:07,027 --> 00:19:08,820
( BOTH SCREAM )

323
00:19:13,450 --> 00:19:16,119
Stand your ground.

324
00:19:36,932 --> 00:19:39,184
I'll take care of you myself.

325
00:19:45,315 --> 00:19:46,316
( GRUNTS )

326
00:19:59,913 --> 00:20:00,997
( SCREAMS )

327
00:20:01,081 --> 00:20:04,751
( GRUNTING )

328
00:20:04,876 --> 00:20:06,920
( GASPING )

329
00:20:10,590 --> 00:20:13,552
Leave this village
and never come back.

330
00:20:27,941 --> 00:20:31,027
( DISTANT CHEERING AND WHISTLING )

331
00:20:36,867 --> 00:20:39,745
( CHEERING )

332
00:20:43,039 --> 00:20:44,791
I knew you'd come.

333
00:20:44,916 --> 00:20:46,251
DOCK: Thank you.

334
00:20:46,376 --> 00:20:48,086
MAN: Painted Lady,
you're the best.

335
00:20:48,211 --> 00:20:51,923
Me and my brothers
really owe you a lot.

336
00:20:52,048 --> 00:20:55,886
Hey, wait a minute,
I know you.

337
00:20:56,011 --> 00:20:58,096
You're not the Painted Lady.

338
00:20:58,221 --> 00:21:01,099
You're that colonial girl.

339
00:21:01,224 --> 00:21:04,811
Yeah, you're the lady
that gave me a fish.

340
00:21:04,936 --> 00:21:06,813
You've been tricking us.

341
00:21:06,938 --> 00:21:09,191
You're a waterbender.

342
00:21:09,316 --> 00:21:10,901
She's a waterbender.

343
00:21:11,026 --> 00:21:13,236
MAN: How dare you act like
our Painted Lady?

344
00:21:13,361 --> 00:21:16,072
( CROWD GRUMBLING )

345
00:21:16,198 --> 00:21:19,701
Maybe she is a waterbender, but
she was just trying to help you.

346
00:21:19,826 --> 00:21:22,412
Because of her, that factory
won't be polluting your river

347
00:21:22,537 --> 00:21:24,206
and the army is gone.

348
00:21:24,331 --> 00:21:26,750
You should be down on your knees
thanking her.

349
00:21:26,875 --> 00:21:29,836
Sokka, it's OK.

350
00:21:29,961 --> 00:21:32,130
I shouldn't have acted like
someone I wasn't

351
00:21:32,255 --> 00:21:33,965
and I shouldn't have
tricked you.

352
00:21:34,090 --> 00:21:36,802
But I felt like I had to
do something.

353
00:21:36,927 --> 00:21:40,013
It doesn't matter if
the Painted Lady is real or not.

354
00:21:40,138 --> 00:21:43,934
Because your problems are real,
and this river is real.

355
00:21:44,059 --> 00:21:46,561
You can't wait around
for someone to help you.

356
00:21:46,686 --> 00:21:48,897
You have to help yourself.

357
00:21:49,022 --> 00:21:52,567
She's right,
but what should we do?

358
00:21:52,692 --> 00:21:55,821
Maybe we can clean
the river.

359
00:21:55,946 --> 00:21:59,074
Yeah, we can clean the river.

360
00:21:59,199 --> 00:22:02,828
( CROWD CHEERING )

361
00:22:02,953 --> 00:22:04,538
DOCK: Thank you.

362
00:22:04,663 --> 00:22:07,707
You know, you're not so bad
for a waterbender.

363
00:22:07,833 --> 00:22:10,252
You wouldn't mind keeping that
a secret, by the way, would you?

364
00:22:10,377 --> 00:22:12,003
No problem.

365
00:22:12,128 --> 00:22:14,381
Keeping my mouth shut is
a personal specialty.

366
00:22:14,506 --> 00:22:17,759
My brother Shoe, on the other
hand, ho, he's a blabbermouth.

367
00:22:17,884 --> 00:22:19,094
( GROANS )

368
00:22:19,219 --> 00:22:21,388
So, Dock, are you gonna
help us clean?

369
00:22:21,513 --> 00:22:24,808
No, ma'am, I'm going to get
my other brother, Bushi.

370
00:22:24,933 --> 00:22:29,062
He loves cleaning rivers.

371
00:22:29,187 --> 00:22:30,897
All right, I'm Bushi.

372
00:22:31,022 --> 00:22:32,899
Let's get some
river cleaning done.

373
00:22:33,024 --> 00:22:35,151
Aha, I knew it.

374
00:22:35,277 --> 00:22:37,028
I knew you were the same guy.

375
00:22:37,153 --> 00:22:39,739
You're the shop owner
and the boat guy.

376
00:22:39,865 --> 00:22:42,826
Oh, you must be talking about
my brothers, Dock and Shoe.

377
00:22:42,951 --> 00:22:44,744
No, I just saw you.

378
00:22:44,870 --> 00:22:46,830
You switched hats and called
yourself a different name.

379
00:22:46,955 --> 00:22:49,207
Oh, you know who does that?

380
00:22:49,332 --> 00:22:51,418
My brother Dock.

381
00:22:51,543 --> 00:22:53,253
He's crazy.

382
00:22:53,378 --> 00:22:56,840
( LAUGHS )

383
00:23:06,558 --> 00:23:09,060
( WATER SPLASHING )

384
00:23:33,084 --> 00:23:35,921
Thank you.

385
00:23:50,060 --> 00:23:53,730
( ♪... )
